{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4awH7ivNeLMeD8yygQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `fetcher` package is now async, and all 8 tests pass (`python3 -m pytest -q`, 0.23s). I didn't commit anything.\n\n**Changes**\n- **`fetcher/client.py`**: `Client(transport=None, retries=3, backoff=0.01, max_concurrency=5)`.\n  - `get` and `close` are now `async`, and `async with` is supported.\n  - `default_transport` is async and uses `asyncio.sleep(0.01)`.\n  - Retries use `asyncio.sleep` with the same exponential backoff, and still retry only on `TransientError`.\n  - `get_many` uses an `asyncio.Semaphore(max_concurrency)` with `gather`, so results keep input order. Per-URL exceptions come back as `FetchError` instances rather than being raised.\n- **`fetcher/aggregate.py`**: `summarize` is `async`, and its return shape is unchanged.\n- **`fetcher/sync.py`** (new): `fetch_all(urls, transport=None)` runs `get_many` through `asyncio.run`.\n- **`tests/test_client.py`**: the three original tests are ported to plain `asyncio.run`, so no new dependency is needed. I added tests for these cases:\n  - a non-transient error is not retried;\n  - output order is kept when completion order differs;\n  - the concurrency cap is respected;\n  - `fetch_all` works both with the default transport and with an injected one.\n\n**Choices I made that you didn't specify**\n- `max_concurrency < 1` raises `ValueError`. A value of 0 would otherwise deadlock.\n- The concurrency limit applies only to `get_many`. Direct calls to `get` are not throttled.\n- `fetch_all` can't be called from inside a running event loop, because `asyncio.run` can't nest. The docstring says so.\n\nI left `.claude/`, `hooks/`, and `input.yaml` untouched."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1513,"cache_read_input_tokens":41872,"cache_creation":{"epheme